WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.070
- What's different about entrepreneurship

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.130
than rap and sports,

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.880
is when you say you're a rapper

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.220
someone's like all right, rap.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.113
And then if you suck,
everyone's like oh you suck.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.110
And when you say you're
a basketball player,

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.420
people are like, at the
YMCA or going to the league?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.560
The one thing I love
about entrepreneurship

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.800
is it's binary.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.660
Either you're gonna win
or you're gonna lose.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.077
(slow music)

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.790
Being a businessman or
woman wasn't cool in 1992.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.273
It was Bill Gates, a fuckin' nerd.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:47.230
So now that everybody wants
to put entrepreneurship

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.460
in their Instagram profile,

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.660
and that's cool in the club,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.570
that is just bazaaro world,

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.630
but that's also done what
sports and rapping has,

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.900
which is everybody wishes they are.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.430
And what's different
about entrepreneurship

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.470
than rap and sports,

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.210
is when you say you're a rapper,

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.560
someone's like, all right, rap.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.670
And then if you suck,

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.255
everyone's like oh you suck.

00:01:12.255 --> 00:01:14.460
And when you say you're
a basketball player,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.850
people are like at the YMCA,
or going to the league?

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.380
But when somebody now says
their an entrepreneur,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.850
it's just accepted.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.470
And we haven't matured into

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.440
are you a successful entrepreneur,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.310
or a wannabe entrepreneur?

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.750
And to be very frank,
I'm concerned about it,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.840
because I think, the one thing
I love about entrepreneurship

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.080
is it's binary,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.130
either you're gonna win
or you're gonna lose.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.850
And I think that there's
a lot of people right now

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.200
that are not built

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.870
with dealing with the emotional baggage

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.113
that comes along with a public loss.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.870
And so I spent a lot of time
with young entrepreneurs

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:51.110
around the mentality of like,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.970
when you lose, are you
ready to take that ridicule,

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:56.430
and what are you gonna do?

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.360
The greatest reason I
believe that we're living

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.660
through such fake
entrepreneurship right now,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.250
is not only is there an enormous
amount of capital in play

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.510
for these 22-25 year olds,

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:07.620
but they're the generation

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.270
that was parented in a way

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.820
that tried to eliminate
losses from the ecosystem.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.083
I mean this is the generation
of eighth place trophies.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.360
My favorite thing that's
going on in society right now

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:27.210
is 45 to 60 year olds
clowning on millennials

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.120
and making fun of them,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.210
and I keep looking at them

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.503
and I keep reminding them
that you parented these kids.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.990
- [Man In Hat] Everybody
gets a trophy right?

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:39.990
- Yeah, and so we've demonized
to these kids losing.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.563
I love losing.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.660
Micro-losing especially,
more than macro-losing

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.150
is incredibly motivating.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.550
I mean there's nothing more fun

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.880
than losing regular season games.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.450
You know, you learn from them.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:56.153
Come the playoffs you'd
like to build on that,

00:02:56.153 --> 00:03:00.800
but yeah, I think adversity
is the foundation of success.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.410
Being born in the Soviet Union,

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.630
living in a studio apartment
with eight family members

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:05.630
when I was a kid.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.650
Going on one and a half
vacations my entire childhood.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:09.900
My parents buying me nothing,

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:10.733
because they didn't have,

00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:13.860
like the money nor the
mindset to do that for me

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.814
is fundamentally the reason

00:03:15.814 --> 00:03:18.750
I'm successful at entrepreneurship.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.550
I'm not scared of anything,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.160
nor do I care about
anybody else's judgment,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.670
which allows me to navigate very quickly,

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.090
and my losses are my losses,

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.620
and my wins are my wins,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.360
and they both feel the same.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.640
When I hear the accolades,
or when I get razzed,

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.270
I basically can't hear them.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.389
I'm just so in love with the process.

00:03:38.389 --> 00:03:42.440
And that's what getting
up off the floor is.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.672
You had no choice,

00:03:43.672 --> 00:03:46.760
it's in your DNA to wanna play.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.240
- I'm wondering what's the message

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.240
to a company that doesn't have innovation

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:55.470
as a core part of their business?

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.303
- They're in trouble.

00:03:56.303 --> 00:03:57.260
- How do they respond?

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.990
- By letting themselves die.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.370
- [Man In Hat] But what do they
do if they don't wanna die?

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.290
- Innovate.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.170
- [Man In Hat] And how do they do that?

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.550
What's the secret?

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.500
- By looking at the leader
of the company in the mirror,

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:11.580
and see if she or he is
capable of innovating.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.770
Everything stems from the top.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.330
If you have a company run by somebody

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.810
who right now is sitting and saying

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.780
well I'm retiring in 18 months,

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.860
and I don't give a shit about innovation,

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.240
you're in trouble.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.023
Or not talented enough
to know how to innovate.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.240
You know how many A's, number ones

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.790
hire a CMO and say you figure it out,

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.720
but they don't even know how to judge it?

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.140
How are you a CEO in 2019,

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:42.040
and don't spend 100
hours to educate yourself

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.980
on how modern communication works

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.953
so that you can judge it
within your own organization?

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.210
Gary, I didn't grow up with this stuff.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:53.210
You didn't grow up driving,
you figured it out.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.560
I know you didn't grow up with it,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.490
but it is your job, it's required of you

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.900
to know how to run your business.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.680
And to me, how your business
markets and communicates

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.140
is as important as you knowing

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.210
how to run the finances of your company.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.440
It's just that some people
don't wanna put in the work

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.030
to get updated on the new platforms

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.460
and the new world,

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.870
and that's to their peril.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.040
The advice that I think will
play for everybody in the room

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.060
regardless of what you do,

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:22.240
including if you're like the PTA president

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:24.210
or thinking about
running for local office,

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.670
like I have no idea what you wanna do

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.180
professionally or personally,

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.720
but the one thing that
has been tried and true

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.550
and I keep things extremely simple,

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.110
is you have to reverse engineer

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.310
the audience you're trying to reach,

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:36.810
and you have to tell them
something that brings them value,

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.520
not you value.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.520
Every single person here

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.280
that is in power to do so,

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.010
needs to go spend the next 100 days

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.880
having phone calls, having dinner,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.500
having breakfast, having drinks

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.340
with every one of their customers

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.510
and they need to listen
to what they care about.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.180
And then they need to go back to the pad

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.993
and cook that meal.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.150
That's all I do.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.070
I read my comments left and right,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.390
I was just talking with your CMO prepping,

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.940
you guys were wrapping up.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.630
And she's like are you always
like this on your phone?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.010
And I was laughing, what I was doing,

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.850
I was reading comments.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.200
Because the qualitative feedback

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.370
is the insight I need
for the next innovation.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:20.250
The amount of people who
hope their customers like

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.410
what they are doing,

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.400
or they're trying to force their customers

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.240
to like what they wanna sell

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.500
is fascinating for me to watch.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.430
- You've talked about this,

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.650
is that people who are dragging down

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:32.590
the culture of a business

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.630
should be, they shouldn't be there.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.620
- I wish most businesses

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.820
were into documenting in coach.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.860
What most businesses are doing is,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.483
Harold's a dick, but his
numbers are remarkable.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.780
That's what's really happening.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.330
That's what I'm referring to.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.300
That if you've got somebody

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.660
who's driving top line revenue,

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.260
or she or he is crushing their numbers,

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:59.690
what most companies are doing

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.220
is they're looking at surface level,

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.800
they're like if we fire Carol,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.240
we're gonna lose those three accounts

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.000
'cause she's so wired in there.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.230
What they don't realize
is the hidden lost revenue

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:12.600
that's happening with Carol or Harold

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.560
destroying the culture,

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.550
and completely messing up the continuity

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.710
and speed of the macro.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.543
- So what do you do,

00:07:20.543 --> 00:07:22.140
from your point of view what do you do

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.990
if you have someone
who's really kickin' ass,

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.890
bringing the numbers in

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:28.723
and they're just a,

00:07:28.723 --> 00:07:31.140
they're a jerk, what do you do with them?

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.430
- What I do, one man's point of view

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.140
is I sit them down.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.290
I look them dead in the face,

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.590
and I say you think I'm joking
because you're delivering,

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.970
but I'm not joking,

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:43.070
and if you can't be a good human being

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.340
I'm going to fire your face.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.250
(laughing)

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.030
- [Man In Hat] That's pretty right there.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:49.863
- That's what I do,

00:07:49.863 --> 00:07:51.800
and I do it, and I do it,

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:54.570
I'm a big shot on stage
now and I'm acting tough,

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.790
I do it in a conversation.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.300
I'm like look, I'm not kidding,

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.870
I know you don't believe me

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.170
because you've worked at other places

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.090
that value dollars,

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:03.270
and I value dollars,

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.730
I just value slow dimes.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.900
So when you deliver on culture,

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.470
the buy in and the macro is remarkable.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:12.630
And what it does for the
business is extraordinary.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.180
I'm a pot committed buyer of this thesis.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.370
That you have to fire the best performers

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:21.410
that are destroying your culture.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.160
(dramatic music)

